  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/zen-browser/desktop/tarball/1.22.2b",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/zen-browser/desktop/zipball/1.22.2b",
  "body": "# Zen Stable Release\n\n\n## Security\n- https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/security/advisories/mfsa2026-90/\n\n## New Features\n- Updated to Firefox 156.0\n- Zen on macOS can now be set to open automatically when the computer starts up, from the Startup section of Settings.\n- Added the following actions to the command bar: 'Expand current view', 'New space', 'Reopen closed tab', 'Duplicate tab', 'Reset pinned tab'.\n\n## Fixes\n- Fixed high-sample-rate FLAC audio in MP4 failing to play on certain video sites.\n- Fixed subtitles not appearing in the Picture-in-Picture window when they are turned on in the video player after the window has already opened.\n- Fixed the find bar becoming permanently unavailable in a tab after reversing the panes in Split View.\n- Fixed some sites failing to load when DNS over HTTPS is enabled and the site does not support HTTPS.\n- Fixed an issue on Windows where Zen could block an auto-hiding taskbar from showing.\n- Fixed the sidebar not hiding if the urlbar is open when compact mode is enabled. ([#13196](https://github.com/zen-browser/desktop/issues/13196))\n- Fixed an issue where cross-space tab routing would freeze the browser under certain conditions. ([#14171](https://github.com/zen-browser/desktop/issues/14171))\n- Fixed cross-device sync losing certain tabs if they are created too quickly ([#15380](https://github.com/zen-browser/desktop/issues/15380))\n- Fixed certain issues related to live folders appearing as active even when they are no tabs showing in them.\n- Other bug fixes and improvements.\n\n## Changes\n- Zen's built-in PDF viewer now starts up to 45% faster.\n- Improved memory and CPU usage when Zen displays large JPEG images scaled down to fit a page.\n- On Windows devices with ARM64 processors, WebRTC video calls may now use hardware H264 decoding instead of falling back to software.\n- Live Folders will now ignore archived issues and pull requests.\n- Improved the look and feel of drag-and-drop interactions for tabs. Specially on MacOS, where the drag-and-drop behavior is now done natively.\n- Folders will now fully-expand if all tabs within them are visible. Folder animations has also been improved for smoother transitions.\n",
